From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sm64ar <sm64ar@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Title screen head, splash logo and game-over backdrop

Puts the title screen's Mario head (Goddard) on the table:

- the head draws in world space and is lit as an object; its hand cursor is
  its own overlay group and is never put in AR mode;
- seams in src/goddard/ar_goddard.h map between the cursor and Goddard's
  world, give the gd camera's view direction and let the host move the
  cursor (pinch input);
- with eye follow on, the eyes follow the cursor also during the head's
  normal animation, but only on frames where the face is as in vanilla's
  still pose (a mask built from the animation);
- the splash logo's overshoot grows up from its floor instead of about its
  centre, and the game-over backdrop is its own overlay group behind the
  head.

Off (the default without gArMode), all of it is vanilla.
